// Example funtion definition
// pub inline fn function_name(parameter1: type1, parameter2: type2) return_type { 
//     ... 
// }

// `pub` is a modifier that decides weather a function is public
// if ommited the function will be private

// `inline` is a modifier that tells the compiler to replece the invocation of the function with the function body diretly

// `fn` is a keyword that signals function declaration, 
// it is followed by the name of the function
// the name of the functuion is followed by `(...)`, where ... are the parameters of the function
// parameters are of a format `parameter: type`

// after `(...)` the function requires a return type, if the function doesn't return anything the return type is `void`

// after the return type there is `{...}` which is a block of statements that will be executed on function call

// to call a function write: `function_name(arg1, arg2)`

// Return type is one of forms:
// - `type`, which indicates that the function return a value of `type`
// - `error!type`, which indicates that the function return an `error` or a value of `type`
// Note that this includes `optional` types via:
// - `?type`, which indicates that the function return an `optional` value of `type`
// - `error!?type`, which indicates that the function return an `error` or an `optional` value of `type`




